A TRAILING `continue` SILENTLY DELETES THE REST OF THE ENCLOSING BLOCK.
THIS IS THE REGRESSION TEST. It was incant/fixits/trailingContinue until
2026-08-28, when the remedy was stepped, blessed by Tony, and the citizen
promoted here.

WHAT THE THREE ARMS ASSERT. Identical shape each: a loop whose last executed
statement is `continue`, then one statement after the loop. All three must
print "arm entered", run three passes, and reach the statement after the loop.

/!\ THE ARM-ENTERED MARKERS ARE THE ANTI-VACUITY CONTROL AND ARE NOT
DECORATION. Without them, "FOR printed nothing" is indistinguishable from "the
FOR arm never ran", which is a completely different defect. The markers prove
the loop ran and the TAIL was eaten.

THE MECHANISM, Tony's own, written when he fixed WhilE (b88f33d): when the last
iteration hits a continue, the loop's `result` is still the continue SENTINEL,
which then propagates to the ENCLOSING block as a continue and pooches it. One
channel carrying two meanings -- "skip this iteration" and "this is the block's
value" -- the second leaking across a boundary the first was never meant to
cross. His word on the WhilE version: NOT AN OPTIONAL FIX.

