/!\ aCTionFOR ALSO CONTINUES EARLIER, at the `restrict` test, AND THAT ARM IS
DELIBERATELY UNTOUCHED -- `result = 0;` runs at the head of every iteration, so
no sentinel is ever in flight there. A blind paste would have been harmless but
the reason would have been wrong. aCTionDO, by contrast, has NO `result = 0;`
at the head of its body, which is precisely why the sentinel survived there.
Same cure, three different reasons. Do not "unify" these by pattern-match.

